# ControlRig Stable Authoring Release Note

Date: 2026-06-30

Status: released to `origin/main`

This release completes the ControlRig stable authoring work that started with
Phase 1 read-only skeleton profiling and recipe-planning evidence, then advanced
through the stable fixture, transaction hardening, binding-only proof, and
reviewed input-default gate.

## Shipped Commits

- `3927bc17` - `controlrig: add stable authoring implementation`
- `f54a54ab` - `controlrig: add stable authoring phase contracts`
- `0415b31b` - `controlrig: add binding proof and input-default gate`
- `0c5738ae` - `controlrig: wire stable authoring release checks`
- `b515622b` - `niagara: mark composite tools python-only`

## What Shipped

- Read-only ControlRig skeleton profile and deterministic recipe-planning
  evidence.
- Deterministic profile-to-recipe compiler with stricter ambiguous alias and
  side-specific bone handling.
- Stable sample/temp-only Piper fixture recipe and binding contract.
- Transaction report hardening for planned/performed/skipped writes and cleanup
  guidance.
- Binding-only AnimBP proof path using existing safe bridge commands.
- Reviewed stable input-default gate for
  `PiperStable_GlobalStableGate_CTRL = 1.0`.
- Phase 1-6 filesystem contracts, live proof artifacts, and release-gate
  integration.

## Verification

- UE 5.6 C++ build: passed.
- ControlRig/AnimBP MCP release gate: passed, `total=32 failed=0`.
- Phase 6 contract: passed.
- Stable input-default promotion check: passed.
- Semantic audit: passed.
- MCP tool parity audit: passed after marking newly rebased Niagara composite
  tools as Python-only.

## Boundaries Held

- No original asset mutation was required.
- Unreal write targets remain constrained to `/Game/_MCP_Temp` or
  `/Game/_MCP_Sample`.
- No runtime/gameplay module was added.
- No solver unit expansion was introduced.
- `UnrealMCP` still has no static C++ dependency on
  `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`.
- MCP-only references are not serialized into generated assets by this flow.

## Deferred

- Solver-unit authoring remains blocked until an explicit allowlist and manual
  approval gate are designed.
- A fresh promoted-state live proof can be captured later if another handoff
  wants current-session live evidence beyond the archived proof.
